From f5971f084a9d204eff13338949beb6b173a3f2ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Randolph <randolph@andestech.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Feb 2025 15:48:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 49/53] swdtb: baudrate: chosen: support baudrate 115200 [Bug
 33409] (#156)

The built-in DTB currently supports a baud rate of 38400. In the ASTv540
official the linux switch to support 115200.

The Linux kernel log will display garbled text until the Linux shell
environment is accessed. The complete log is now displayed correctly
after the modification.

Add 1 additional space to the allocated string length in
replace_serial_string() to ensure the string displays completely
when the DTB is reverted to DTS.

Add a conditional preprocessor to check whether USE_TINY_PRINTF is
enabled or not for the simple_itoa() function.

Signed-off-by: Randolph <randolph@andestech.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gitea.andestech.com/RD-SW/u-boot.official/pulls/156
Reviewed-by: Leo Yu-Chi Liang <ycliang@andestech.com>
Reviewed-by: Alex Chun-Ju Lin <alex749@andestech.com>
Reviewed-by: Tim Shih-Ting OuYang <tim609@andestech.com>
